1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
This Reel has a great hook, a strong ending, and an eighteen-second desert in the middle where everyone left.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:10,000
The desert: one locked shot, one energy level, no new information for eighteen seconds. Viewers don’t leave because it’s bad. They leave because nothing signals that staying pays.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Deserts hide in talking-head stories, in cooking mid-sections, in “step two” of every tutorial. The tell: you can scrub ten seconds and miss nothing.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Three desert-breakers. Move a reveal into the middle. Change the frame — angle, insert, text — every four seconds. Or just cut it. Forty seconds of good beats sixty with a desert.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Save this, then scrub your last three posts and find the desert. It’s there. Mine was twenty-two seconds long and I defended it at the time.

